es of shock an…", "summary": "Young age without typical risk factors makes pancreatitis less likely. This weakly argues against B4 and supports B1/B2."}], "differential_history": [{"top": [["B1", 0.529], ["B1.1", 0.289], ["B3", 0.199]]}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": true, "reason": "Hypotension (80/40 mmHg) and tachycardia (110 bpm) indicate shock, a universal instability marker requiring immediate intervention.", "required_actions": ["Initiate aggressive intravenous fluid resuscitation", "Monitor for signs of ongoing haemorrhage or deterioration", "Prepare for potential surgical intervention if bleeding source is identified"]}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "[static mode override] Active emergency interrupt due to shock markers (hypotension, tachycardia) requires immediate intervention prioritization over diagnostic refinement — emergency_override suppressed in static_diagnosis_qa mode"}, "turn_budget_used": 1, "estimated_remaining_value": 1.25, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.28877005347593576, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely the diagnosis?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Ectopic implantation of a blastocyst"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Inflammation of the pancreas"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Obstruction of blood flow through the hepatic vein"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Obstruction of the common bile duct by radio-opaque stones"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Vascular ectasia within the liver"}], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phenotypes": "{'Chronic pancreatitis', 'Acute pancreatitis'}", "mode_policy": {"benchmark_purity": true, "allow_external_knowledge": true}, "answer_option_mapping": {}, "tool_use_log": [], "root_revision_needed": false, "max_tree_depth": 3, "reasoning_ledger": {"anchor": {"hypothesis": "B1", "t": 0, "posterior_at_ancho